# ouroboros#164: a function assigning a module-level TENSOR global. The
# per-function tensor inference declared a LOCAL AotTensor of the same name,
# so the body read its own empty shadow and never wrote the module value
# (before round 126 a raw gcc type error; after it a runtime shape error).
# The module's tensor names are now known before any function is emitted
# and a plain assign to one is outward. (A `local m` tensor shadow of a
# module tensor is a named refusal -- tensor-classified shadows live in C
# variables, not the env -- so the control here is a second module tensor
# that the function does not touch.)
a is [1, 2]
m is add of [a, a]
define bump() as:
    m is add of [m, a]
    return 0
print of m
bump of null
print of m
bump of null
print of m
n is add of [a, [10, 10]]
print of n
bump of null
print of n
print of m
